cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these certificates or verifiers, please cite this release."
title: "MathIS Sidon Frontier: Exact Symmetric and Two-Sided Certificates"
authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Ariel M."
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/FromAriel/mathis-sidon-frontier"
abstract: >-
  Exact symmetric and asymmetric two-sided Sidon smoothing certificates,
  standalone standard-library Python verifiers and reproducible preservation.
  Version 1.4.0 adds a compact centered-box witness with 1024 kernels at
  M=2048 and L=8, proving sqrt(ab) < 471404576987/500000000000 =
  0.942809153974 in the original Hou-Zhao finite symmetric model. Exact replay
  reconstructs all 16385 covers and energy values without a numerical solver.
  Earlier R9, R16 and two-sided packages retain their historical scope.
  Hou-Zhao, Akwei, Chen and classical optimization/filter methods receive
  explicit attribution. No current record, significant new generic theorem,
  global optimality, finite-rate law, exponent advance or solution of Erdos
  Problem 30 is claimed. Development and review used AI-assisted workflows.
keywords:
  - Sidon sets
  - additive combinatorics
  - exact rational certificate
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Mathematical Integrity System
license: MIT
